cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  spire-rmf-testbench: a reproducible SPIFFE/SPIRE testbench for
  NIST SP 800-53 evidence generation
message: >-
  If you use this software or its evidence artifacts, please cite it
  using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Samuel
    family-names: Howard
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Ridge4/spire-rmf-testbench'
abstract: >-
  Infrastructure-as-code and evidence artifacts for a SPIFFE/SPIRE
  deployment on Amazon EKS, built inside a private-only VPC to emulate a
  restricted federal cloud enclave. The testbench generates the evidence
  a federal assessor would need to validate ephemeral workload identity
  against NIST SP 800-53 controls, including authenticator management
  (IA-5), cryptographic key storage (SC-12), service identification
  (IA-9), transmission confidentiality (SC-8), and audit logging (AU-2,
  AU-3). Terraform builds the VPC, EKS cluster, RDS datastore, and KMS
  key management; Helm values configure SPIRE; captured logs and
  configuration under evidence/ support each control claim.
keywords:
  - SPIFFE
  - SPIRE
  - workload identity
  - zero trust architecture
  - NIST SP 800-53
  - Risk Management Framework
  - Kubernetes
  - Amazon EKS
  - FedRAMP
  - cloud security
  - compliance evidence
license: Apache-2.0